{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-25",
  "title": "Epocrates Overview",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Epocrates Overview"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Epocrates is a widely used mobile medical reference application designed for healthcare professionals. Here are the key points about Epocrates:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Overview"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-4",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "It provides healthcare professionals with access to clinical information at the point of care[2]."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-5",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Epocrates is the #1 medical reference app and has served clinical content to more than a million users[1]."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "History"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-8",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Founded in 1998, Epocrates initially ran on Palm Pilot devices[2]."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-9",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "It became one of the first medical apps on the iPhone platform[1][2]."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In 2013, Epocrates was acquired by athenahealth for about $293 million[2]."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Features"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The free version of Epocrates includes:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-18",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-14",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Drug information and interaction checker"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-15",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Pill identification tool"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-16",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Clinical practice guidelines"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-17",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Medical calculators and tables[4][5]"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The premium version (Epocrates+) offers additional features such as:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-25",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-20",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Disease information"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-21",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Alternative medicine content"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-22",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "ICD-10 and CPT codes"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-23",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Infectious disease treatment guidance"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-24",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Laboratory information[4][7]"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-26",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "User Base"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-29",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-27",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Over 1 million healthcare professionals worldwide use Epocrates[6]."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-28",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "It's used by an estimated 40% of physicians in the United States[2]."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-30",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Accessibility"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-33",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-31",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Available as a mobile app for iOS and Android devices[4]."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-32",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Some content can be accessed offline[3]."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-34",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Epocrates is designed to assist healthcare providers in making informed decisions about drug interactions, medical calculations, diagnosis, and treatment options, ultimately supporting point-of-care decision-making[2][6]."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-35",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "How Epocrates Keeps Data Up-to-date"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The data in the Epocrates database comes from a variety of reputable sources, including pharmaceutical companies, clinical studies, government agencies, and medical literature. The primary sources for drug information and clinical guidelines include:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **FDA and Other Regulatory Agencies**: Epocrates relies on data from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) and other international regulatory agencies to provide accurate and up-to-date information on drug approvals, safety updates, and labeling changes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **Pharmaceutical Companies**: Drug manufacturers provide detailed information about their products, including dosing, indications, contraindications, side effects, and drug interactions. This information is critical for ensuring that healthcare professionals have accurate data."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-39",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **Medical Literature and Clinical Guidelines**: Epocrates incorporates information from peer-reviewed medical journals, clinical trials, and evidence-based guidelines. These sources help ensure that the app provides current and clinically relevant information."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-40",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. **Clinical Pharmacologists and Medical Experts**: Epocrates employs or consults with clinical pharmacologists, physicians, and other medical experts to review and validate the data. This expert input ensures that the content is both accurate and practically useful for healthcare providers."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-41",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "How Epocrates Keeps Its Database Up to Date:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-42",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **Regular Updates**: Epocrates conducts regular updates to its database, often on a weekly or monthly basis, to incorporate new drug approvals, safety warnings, and changes to clinical guidelines. This ensures that users have access to the most current information available."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-43",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **Real-Time Alerts**: For critical updates, such as drug recalls or new safety warnings, Epocrates can push notifications or alerts directly to users. This feature helps healthcare professionals stay informed about urgent changes that could impact patient care."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-44",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **Collaboration with Regulatory Agencies**: Epocrates maintains close relationships with regulatory agencies like the FDA, enabling them to quickly integrate new information into their platform."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-45",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. **User Feedback**: Healthcare professionals using the app can provide feedback or report issues, which helps Epocrates identify any gaps or errors in the information. This feedback loop is essential for maintaining the accuracy and relevance of the database."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-46",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. **Dedicated Content Teams**: Epocrates has dedicated teams responsible for curating and maintaining the content. These teams review the latest medical literature, updates from regulatory agencies, and other relevant sources to ensure that the database reflects the most up-to-date and reliable information."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-47",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "By relying on these sources and processes, Epocrates ensures that its database remains a trusted and valuable resource for healthcare professionals."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-48",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Citations:"
        }
      ]
    },
